## Build Mode Complete

**PR #2:** https://github.com/mihirathale98/e2e-iter-todo/pull/2

**What was built:** A Python CLI todo manager (`todo-cli`) with:
- 5 commands: `add`, `list`, `complete`, `delete`, `show`
- SQLite storage with parameterized queries
- Priority levels (high/medium/low) with colored Rich output
- Natural language due dates: `today`, `tomorrow`, `+3d`, `+2w`, ISO format
- Filtering by priority and due date, sorting by priority/due/created
- Overdue highlighting, empty state messages, actionable error messages
- `--no-color` flag + `NO_COLOR` env var, `TODO_DB_PATH` env var override
- Structured file logging

**Quality signals:**
- 53 tests passing in 0.13s
- Composite eval score: 0.8013 (hygiene 0.98, growth 0.63)
- ruff clean, mypy strict clean
- 10/10 adversarial QA acceptance criteria verified
- 0 critical code review issues

**Stack:** Single production dependency (`typer[all]>=0.12.0`), everything else stdlib (sqlite3, datetime, pathlib, logging).
